msgstr ""
"Rebrote (la vegetación aumentó desde la fecha de referencia — no es en "
"absoluto una señal de quema)"

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/processing/optical/spectral-indices.md:43
msgid "−0.25 to 0.1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/processing/optical/spectral-indices.md:43
msgid "Unburned"
msgstr "Sin quemar"

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/processing/optical/spectral-indices.md:43
msgid "0.1 to 0.27"
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/processing/optical/spectral-indices.md:43
msgid "Low severity"
msgstr "Severidad baja"

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/processing/optical/spectral-indices.md:43
msgid "0.27 to 0.44"
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/processing/optical/spectral-indices.md:43
msgid "Moderate-low severity"
msgstr "Severidad moderada-baja"

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/processing/optical/spectral-indices.md:43
msgid "0.44 to 0.66"
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/processing/optical/spectral-indices.md:43
msgid "Moderate-high severity"
msgstr "Severidad moderada-alta"

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/processing/optical/spectral-indices.md:43
msgid "> 0.66"
msgstr ""

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/processing/optical/spectral-indices.md:43
msgid "High severity"
msgstr "Severidad alta"

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/processing/optical/spectral-indices.md:364
msgid ""
"**Use it for**: post-fire burn severity mapping, fire perimeter delineation,"
" forest recovery monitoring (watch dNBR trend back toward zero over "
"subsequent years)."
msgstr ""
"**Úselo para**: mapeo de severidad de quemas posincendio, delimitación del "
"perímetro de incendios, monitoreo de la recuperación forestal (observe cómo "
"la tendencia del dNBR vuelve hacia cero a lo largo de los años siguientes)."

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/processing/optical/spectral-indices.md:368
msgid "Snow & moisture"
msgstr "Nieve y humedad"

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/processing/optical/spectral-indices.md:375
msgid ""
"**NDSI** (Hall 1995): `(Green - SWIR1) / (Green + SWIR1)`. Snow is highly "
"reflective in visible light but absorbs SWIR strongly — values above `0.4` "
"typically indicate snow cover. Also useful for discriminating snow from "
"clouds (both are bright in visible light, but clouds don't show the same "
"SWIR absorption)."
msgstr ""
"**NDSI** (Hall 1995): `(Green - SWIR1) / (Green + SWIR1)`. La nieve es muy "
"reflectante en la luz visible pero absorbe con fuerza el SWIR — los valores "
"superiores a `0.4` suelen indicar cobertura de nieve. También es útil para "
"distinguir la nieve de las nubes (ambas son brillantes en la luz visible, "
"pero las nubes no muestran la misma absorción en el SWIR)."

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/processing/optical/spectral-indices.md:380
msgid ""
"**NDMI** (Wilson & Sader 2002): `(NIR - SWIR1) / (NIR + SWIR1)`. Sensitive "
"to canopy water content — positive values indicate moist, well-watered "
"vegetation; useful for drought stress monitoring alongside NDVI (a canopy "
"can still look \"green\" on NDVI while already water-stressed on NDMI)."
msgstr ""
"**NDMI** (Wilson & Sader 2002): `(NIR - SWIR1) / (NIR + SWIR1)`. Sensible al"
" contenido de agua del dosel — los valores positivos indican vegetación "
"húmeda y bien regada; útil para el monitoreo del estrés por sequía junto con"
" el NDVI (un dosel puede seguir viéndose \"verde\" en el NDVI mientras ya "
"sufre estrés hídrico en el NDMI)."

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/processing/optical/spectral-indices.md:386
msgid "Transforms and general-purpose tools"
msgstr "Transformaciones y herramientas de propósito general"

#: ../../home/claude/work/docs_audit/docs_out/processing/optical/spectral-indices.md:43
